    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d923">

                <pb facs="1084" n="988" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg988"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1125.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    relative to the property of the Home Mission Board of the Southern Baptist
                    Convention in Habana, I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of your note
                    of the 5th instant, in which you say that you are in receipt of a telegram from
                    Her Majesty’s acting consul-general in Habana, stating that an attempt has been
                    made by a man named Sanchez to extort money from the Joerg Mission in connection
                    with the will of the late Dr. Belot.</p>
                <p>A copy of your above-mentioned note has been sent to the chairman of the Home
                    Mission Board of the Southern Baptist Convention for the information of those
                    concerned.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
